<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ranjit Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Maharaja Ranjit Singh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ranjit Singh was the founder and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, who lived from 1780 to 1839. Born into the Sukerchakia <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/misl">Misl</a>, he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> in 1799 and united the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-confederacy">Sikh confederacies</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> under his rule. He built a modernised army and expanded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshawar">Peshawar</a>, but his death was followed by succession crises that weakened the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh.jpg" alt="Ranjit Singh" width="279" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Colonel James Skinner (1778-1841) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharaj_Ranjit_Singh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
